@host = http://localhost:5171

### Register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "SuperSecret123"
}

### Login (Duende IdentityServer's standard OAuth2 token endpoint — note the
### form-urlencoded body, not JSON. offline_access is what makes it return a
### refresh_token; api1 is what makes the access_token work on /api/secure/*.)
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=demo-client&username=alice&password=SuperSecret123&scope=openid profile roles api1 offline_access

### Call a protected endpoint (replace TOKEN with access_token from Login)
GET {{host}}/api/secure/me
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Admin-only endpoint — 403 for alice; log in as admin/Admin123! (seeded on
### startup in Development, see Program.cs) to get a 200 here instead.
GET {{host}}/api/secure/admin-only
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Refresh (replace REFRESH_TOKEN with refresh_token from Login — rotates on every use)
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id=demo-client&refresh_token=REFRESH_TOKEN

### Revoke (replace REFRESH_TOKEN)
POST {{host}}/connect/revocation
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=demo-client&token=REFRESH_TOKEN&token_type_hint=refresh_token

### Discovery document — what a real OAuth2/OIDC client uses to find all of
### the above endpoints automatically instead of hardcoding them.
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
